Today I solved leetcode question 2225: Find players with Zero or Losses.

Description: It states that we are given an array of arrays with size 2.
              Where first index is the player who won and second index is the player who lost.
              So we are told to return an array with size 2 of arrays. In first array we must include players with 0 losses and second array should have players with 1 losses.
              eg- matches=[[1,2],[2,3],[1,3]]
                  ans=[[1],[2,3]]

Solution: First we create a hashmap with key as an integer and value as an array of size 2.
          In key we will store player number and in array we will store his wins and losses at index 0 and 1 respectively.
          Now we will create answer array with 2 arrays in it.
          Then we will iterate through hash map and check for players who have 0 and 1 losses.
          Then we will just add players with 0 losses to first array and players with losses 2 to second array.
          At last we will sort both arrays and we will return our answer.
